        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T18:01:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now we dont\u0027 have any barriers to support non-coherent reads. Is this required for some, all, or none of the implementation in Vulkan?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "457414f6c922889ec1cff7e79381f06b9bdd44b7",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db2a128b_d53663f6",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T18:09:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Vulkan will need a barrier before each draw that will read the dst",
      "parentUuid": "80b3ba77_83a47f29",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "457414f6c922889ec1cff7e79381f06b9bdd44b7",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fa7cdd9_67530666",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T18:24:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Greg is correct that barriers are required for dst reads regardless. In the case of non-coherent advanced blending, we must consult Vulkan physical device properties to see what level of support we have and operate accordingly.\n\nSee VkPhysicalDeviceBlendOperationAdvancedFeaturesEXT::advancedBlendCoherentOperations (https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/latest/man/html/VK_EXT_blend_operation_advanced.html#_description) which informs memory dependency requirements.\n\nThere is a comment in `ShaderInfo.cpp` that references the relevant task (b/239726010 \"Support fixed state advanced blend modes and blend barriers\"; https://skia.googlesource.com/skia.git/+/refs/heads/main/src/gpu/graphite/ShaderInfo.cpp#599). Added comments regarding this here and to `ShaderCaps` to make clear that graphite needs to implement this still.",
      "parentUuid": "db2a128b_d53663f6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "457414f6c922889ec1cff7e79381f06b9bdd44b7",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c202bf9d_b7868c5f",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T18:29:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI VkPhysicalDeviceBlendOperationAdvancedFeaturesEXT::advancedBlendCoherentOperations is only important if we are using that extension which allows you to specify the advanced blends as actual pipeline blend state. When using input attachments/barriers we will always have non-coherent blending.",
      "parentUuid": "7fa7cdd9_67530666",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 51
      },
